# Build context exclusions for the container image.
#
# The important one is `target/`. Without this file `COPY . .` drags the host's
# build tree into the image, and the Dockerfile stages the binary with
# `find cli/target -type f -name literouter` — which then has several stale
# binaries from earlier local builds to choose from. The image ends up shipping
# whichever one `find` happened to return first, which is how a build that
# succeeds can still produce an image missing the feature you just added.
#
# `.git` is excluded because it is large and the image never needs history.
# `web/node_modules` is excluded because `web/dist` is committed and is what the
# C++ build embeds; the toolchain never runs npm.

# Host build trees (all workspace members)
target/
**/target/
build/
**/build/

# Version control and editor state
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Front-end dependencies and tooling caches; web/dist IS needed, so it stays.
web/node_modules/
web/.vite/
**/node_modules/

# Local runtime state and scratch files
*.log
*.pid
*.tmp*
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.mcpp/
